# F5h: the pairs fused arm again (B, second repeat).
# Duration (estimate): 20-30 min (reset 1-3 min, engine build 10-20 min on a warm cache, the four tests 10-15 min). Audits are OFF.
# Read: the [PACKED-PHASE] lines (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early draft; gap) and [PACKED-PUBLISH] medians at 4 live in concurrent4_steady: the round wall, commits (eager arms about 38 ms; fused arms about 2 ms), early_draft (the fused arms carry 0-3 ms of T_proj device work here), the per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT] mean; the coding decode_tok_s. Judge every pair of arms PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run (a busy host skews host phases 10-20%) and repeat before believing a small gap. Then offline: python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <eager arm results> <fused arm results> --users 0,1,2,3 --position-keyed --strict-concurrent-prefixes (exit 0 identical, 1 a different draft, 2 too few shared positions): the fused commit must not change a single draft K/V byte, so every user accepted-prefix sequence must be IDENTICAL. SOFT: the numbers are the product.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card fused-commit window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fcommit and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are
# the driver's, on the allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image F0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: set it (in every template of the window) to the tag the driver picks.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-fcommit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
